{
  "name": "profile-det (settings profile sub-page, operator + builder, autosave onblur, native selects exercised, fast-fail on data-dependent)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against routes/settings/Profile.svelte + ui/select/Select.svelte + ui/dialog/{Dialog,ConfirmDialog}.svelte + routes/Settings.svelte.",
    "The profile is backed by SemanticMemory under __user__ (profile_schema.rs). The seed sets preferences.language=fr but NOT name/role, so name+role start empty and are filled here.",
    "profile-select-* are native <select> (Select.svelte passes data-testid onto the <select>); each is exercised with selectOption using a valid static option value. The onchange handler persists the value via saveKey.",
    "profile-radio-* testids sit on the RadioGroup container; individual RadioItem elements carry no testid and there is no radio-option primitive, so the group is asserted present only (an option cannot be picked).",
    "profile-integ-github / profile-compliance-rgpd are <button role=checkbox> (Checkbox.svelte), NOT <input>; they are toggled with click (setChecked requires a native input and would throw).",
    "settings-saved-hint renders whenever the sub-page is not dirty (Settings.svelte). Profile autosaves on blur so it is never dirty, hence the hint is a deterministic present-assert.",
    "Autosave: consecutive fill steps focus the next field, which blurs (and saves) the previous one; the first selectOption focus blurs and saves the goals textarea.",
    "showEnrichmentBanner is derived (calibrationDone AND tier2 has an empty field). It is treated as best-effort: observed by screenshot only, never hard-asserted and never used as a click target, so no step can fail on it.",
    "Profile.svelte has zero uiMode-conditional rendering; the builder pass asserts mode-invariance of the same fields."
  ],
